Key Insights
Built a complete user funnel for the Save journey.
Calculated stage-wise user conversion.
Identified the largest drop-off point in the onboarding process.
Measured the median completion time between the first and final stages.
Documented assumptions required due to limited dataset availability.
Assumptions

The SQL analysis was developed based on the following assumptions:

Every event record represents a valid user action.
Event timestamps are accurate and stored in chronological order.
Users follow the intended funnel sequence.
Duplicate events are handled using COUNT(DISTINCT user_id).
Only users completing both the first and final stages are included in completion-time analysis.
The provided dataset is complete and contains no missing event records.
